# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs four device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), and html
# for its ask_user and show_html tools (the html command). The recipe engine
# lets an npm user build an image FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-core 77420975d2e00045a4afdbd148c409e4435346b7fe01901723bbdd8a365d59ca
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-dollyfile 0bce0656ec37a01be40584a1be08b6540a061abe0dbb308c805495458aa2bf17
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-posix ee863b1c77e6b47d79bdcd1b2d5d278e6ad9d84771d3e2b61149a07d592fa163
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-display 216c8c7a3849e5ab30f61b2763c47713d0e65812227f5afe86b23cbcd24ade8e
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-curl 5493b1f90354a20ebabbb8e2cb36603375218167a79cb4aed91f6e88df0e4360
